1
00:00:00,700 --> 00:00:05,309
This is a short guide to the CLEETS knowledge graph visualisations:

2
00:00:05,359 --> 00:00:12,056
two web pages that let you read CLEETS-KG without reading its Turtle file.

3
00:00:12,106 --> 00:00:18,782
CLEETS-KG is published as a Turtle file: 96,479 triples, about six megabytes of text.

4
00:00:18,832 --> 00:00:24,480
Every fact is in there, but a file like this shows one triple at a time.

5
00:00:24,530 --> 00:00:29,070
To see how the eight source datasets meet in the ontology,

6
00:00:29,120 --> 00:00:32,473
or to find every observation about Cardiff,

7
00:00:32,523 --> 00:00:37,458
you would have to write queries or scroll for a very long time.

8
00:00:37,508 --> 00:00:45,896
The two pages do that reading for you.

9
00:00:45,946 --> 00:00:48,506
The landing page offers two views.

10
00:00:48,556 --> 00:00:52,421
The dataset map shows the ontology and its sources.

11
00:00:52,471 --> 00:00:56,643
The entity explorer shows every individual in the data.

12
00:00:56,693 --> 00:01:00,097
Both are generated from the same Turtle file,

13
00:01:00,147 --> 00:01:07,863
and every figure they show was cross-checked against it with SPARQL.

14
00:01:07,913 --> 00:01:14,561
The dataset map draws the ontology in VOWL notation, the same notation used by WebVOWL.

15
00:01:14,611 --> 00:01:20,643
Circles are classes, sized by the number of individuals they have in the graph.

16
00:01:20,693 --> 00:01:22,568
Rectangles are datatypes.

17
00:01:22,618 --> 00:01:26,340
Arrows are properties, labelled with their names.

18
00:01:26,390 --> 00:01:33,269
The coloured boxes are the dataset records and the diamonds are the derivation activities.

19
00:01:33,319 --> 00:01:44,429
These are an addition to the notation: they show where the data in each class comes from.

20
00:01:44,479 --> 00:01:48,664
Select a dataset and the map highlights what it contributes.

21
00:01:48,714 --> 00:01:54,805
The public charging device statistics (EVCI9001) become 594 charger-count observations,

22
00:01:54,855 --> 00:01:56,852
one per district and quarter.

23
00:01:56,902 --> 00:02:01,298
The reading at the top says where the dataset meets the others:

24
00:02:01,348 --> 00:02:07,015
with the vehicle licensing table (VEH0132) in the keepers-per-charger derivation,

25
00:02:07,065 --> 00:02:12,520
and with the StatsWales population in chargers per hundred thousand residents.

26
00:02:12,570 --> 00:02:21,796
Click any node for its definition, its restrictions, and the shapes that validate it.

27
00:02:21,846 --> 00:02:28,321
The schematic view is the same information as a fixed wiring diagram: the sources on the left,

28
00:02:28,371 --> 00:02:33,111
the grouped individuals in the middle, and the ontology on the right.

29
00:02:33,161 --> 00:02:40,596
It does not move, so it is the view to use in print or in a slide.

30
00:02:40,646 --> 00:02:46,907
The entity explorer draws all 17,068 individuals and the 51,838 links between them.

31
00:02:46,957 --> 00:02:50,025
The layout follows what the entities are.

32
00:02:50,075 --> 00:02:55,728
The knowledge-graph record and the eight dataset records sit in the middle.

33
00:02:55,778 --> 00:02:59,225
The 67 quarters form the inner ring, in order.

34
00:02:59,275 --> 00:03:02,419
The 22 Welsh districts form the next ring,

35
00:03:02,469 --> 00:03:06,981
each with a disc of its observations and population figures.

36
00:03:07,031 --> 00:03:13,292
The 296 English districts form the outer ring with their population density series.

37
00:03:13,342 --> 00:03:22,476
Links that leave a cluster are drawn as bundles, as wide as the number of links they stand for.

38
00:03:22,526 --> 00:03:26,655
Selecting a dataset fades everything it does not touch.

39
00:03:26,705 --> 00:03:31,215
With the battery-electric vehicle counts (VEH0132) selected,

40
00:03:31,265 --> 00:03:36,534
you see at once that they sit in every Welsh district for 57 quarters,

41
00:03:36,584 --> 00:03:40,789
between late 2011 and late 2025, and nowhere in England.

42
00:03:40,839 --> 00:03:50,116
The derived keeperships per thousand residents and keepers per charger light up with them.

43
00:03:50,166 --> 00:03:54,371
Search finds any entity by its label or its identifier (IRI).

44
00:03:54,421 --> 00:04:00,789
Selecting Cardiff zooms to its disc and opens its record: the district code, the two labels,

45
00:04:00,839 --> 00:04:03,231
and 289 links grouped by predicate.

46
00:04:03,281 --> 00:04:07,416
Every link is a button, so you can walk the graph from here.

47
00:04:07,466 --> 00:04:15,717
This one is the number of public charge points per hundred thousand residents in Cardiff in the fourth quarter of 2019:

48
00:04:15,767 --> 00:04:21,449
twelve point six, with nine links of its own.

49
00:04:21,499 --> 00:04:27,499
Neighbourhood mode isolates the selected entity with its neighbours and names every link.

50
00:04:27,549 --> 00:04:33,005
This derived observation has its district, its quarter, the property it observes,

51
00:04:33,055 --> 00:04:37,832
the derivation that produced it, the two datasets it was computed from,

52
00:04:37,882 --> 00:04:40,415
and the fingerprint of the source row.

53
00:04:40,465 --> 00:04:45,241
This is the view that answers the question a Turtle file makes hardest:

54
00:04:45,291 --> 00:04:51,249
what is connected to this thing, and how.

55
00:04:51,299 --> 00:04:57,243
The legend switches entity types on and off, the relations menu does the same for predicates,

56
00:04:57,293 --> 00:05:02,399
and the layout toggle swaps the structured arrangement for a force-directed one.

57
00:05:02,449 --> 00:05:06,266
Everything you see is drawn from the data at a fixed commit,

58
00:05:06,316 --> 00:05:13,129
which is printed at the foot of each page.

59
00:05:13,179 --> 00:05:16,019
Both pages, the scripts that build them,

60
00:05:16,069 --> 00:05:20,427
and the checks that verify them are in the GitHub repository.

61
00:05:20,477 --> 00:05:28,613
Rebuilding from the Turtle file takes about a minute, so the pages can follow the graph as it grows.
